# One line ending everywhere: text files are stored and checked out with LF
# whatever core.autocrlf says, so the working tree, `git archive` and the
# source zip agree on every machine (rustfmt writes LF as well).
* text=auto eol=lf
# cmd.exe misreads labels and `goto` in batch files with bare LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Snapshot cases are compared byte for byte: sources keep CRLF, a lone CR,
# BOMs and invalid UTF-8 on purpose, and expected.md must match exactly.
tests/snapshots/** -text
# HELP.md holds a raw CR in its "Metadata values" bullet; with `text` set the
# bytes stay exactly as committed.
docs/help/*.md text eol=lf
HELP.md text eol=lf
